      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8cc20412-73ea-5580-b81b-b77cfba9bba9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Video Entertainment Unlimited, Golden West Broadcasting, National Subscription Television, Oak Industries, Chartwell Enterprises\n- Products/Services: VEU, ONTV, ON Subscription Television\n- People: Norman Lear, A. Jerrold Perenchio\n- Places: Oklahoma City, Atlanta, Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex\n- Systems: subscription television, scrambled UHF service\n- Organizations: KAUT-TV, WVEU, KNBN\n\nFacts:\n- VEU (Video Entertainment Unlimited) was an American subscription television channel owned by Golden West Broadcasting.\n- VEU was similar to ONTV, which was another scrambled UHF subscription television service.\n- VEU was carried by stations including KAUT-TV in Oklahoma City, WVEU in Atlanta, and KNBN in the Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex.\n- ONTV was later known as ON Subscription Television from 1983 until its shutdown in 1985.\n- ONTV was an American subscription television service owned by National Subscription Television.\n- National Subscription Television was a joint venture between Oak Industries, Chartwell Enterprises, and media executive A. Jerrold Perenchio.\n- Oak Industries manufactured satellite and pay television decoders and equipment.\n- Chartwell Enterprises was owned by Norman Lear.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "4c643a61-c274-56de-a856-e357cb83b7ee",
        "text": "Page: VEU. Sentence: VEU (Video Entertainment Unlimited) was an American subscription television channel owned by Golden West Broadcasting.\nPage: VEU. Sentence: The channel was similar to ONTV, another scrambled UHF service, and was carried by many stations including KAUT-TV in Oklahoma City, WVEU in Atlanta and KNBN in the Dallas/Fort Worth Metroplex.\nPage: ONTV (pay TV). Sentence: ONTV (later known as ON Subscription Television from 1983 until its shutdown in 1985) is a defunct American subscription television service that was owned by National Subscription Television, a joint venture between Oak Industries (a manufacturer of satellite and pay television decoders and equipment), Chartwell Enterprises (owned by Norman Lear) and media executive A. Jerrold Perenchio.",
